# Product UI

- Read `docs/PRODUCT.md`, `docs/SCOPE.md`, `docs/FEATURE_STATUS.md`, and `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` before changing user-facing UI.
- Use **KorKru / ก่อครู** and the adaptable line **“ก่อ…โดยครู”**; do not lock “ก่อการเรียนรู้ โดยครู” as the permanent slogan.
- Write user-facing copy in clear Thai. Keep code identifiers and standard technical terms in English.
- Do not present mock analytics, invoices, usage, pricing, compliance, security, or unfinished actions as real.
- State clearly which answers are auto-graded and which require teacher review.
- Keep forms keyboard-accessible with visible labels, useful errors, and pending states.
- Respect color contrast and `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Use existing UI primitives and visual tokens before introducing one-off patterns.

## Responsive UI

- Treat responsive behavior as part of the definition of done for every new or changed page, component, button, control, overlay, and UI-affecting function.
- Support desktop, iPad/tablet in portrait and landscape, and phone in portrait and landscape. Do not rely on hover, one orientation, or one viewport width.
- Add breakpoints where content actually stops fitting or reading well, not just at named-device widths. A landscape phone must not accidentally receive a crowded tablet/desktop layout.
- Keep primary content and actions visible and close to what they affect. Reflow, wrap, stack, or change navigation form as space shrinks; never hide an essential action without an accessible alternative.
- Prevent unintended page-level horizontal scrolling, overlapping controls, clipped text, and actions covered by fixed UI. Confine genuinely wide content to a clearly scrollable region.
- Let Thai labels, validation messages, realistic long content, and enlarged text wrap safely. Truncate only non-essential text and keep the full value accessible.
- Keep touch targets comfortable (normally at least 44 x 44 CSS px), separate adjacent actions, and give icon-only controls accessible labels. Do not depend on hover alone.
- Preserve logical keyboard order, visible focus, expected Enter/Space/Escape behavior, modal focus containment, and focus restoration.
- Keep dialogs, sheets, menus, popovers, and sticky/fixed controls inside the visible viewport. Account for safe-area insets, browser chrome, orientation changes, and the on-screen keyboard; allow internal scrolling when needed.
- Verify loading, empty, error, permission, pending, and confirmation states at every supported size, not only the happy path.
- Validate changed UI with realistic long Thai content by resizing continuously from a narrow phone through tablet to wide desktop, in both orientations and at enlarged text/zoom. Also inspect the component in its narrowest supported container.
- Responsive acceptance requires no overlap, clipping, unintended page scroll, unreachable action, obscured focus, or disruptive layout jump at intermediate widths. Browser simulation does not replace required physical-device or SEB testing; record unavailable device checks as pending.
